ps://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ixcg2jfvljshf3p7jhmt77ee/bafkreibonhtoettloqgotoiuxhhnyjdx3nzc3ws6zebdh4x7s4lboi7rae", "associated": {"activitySubscription": {"allowSubscriptions": "followers"}}, "labels": [], "createdAt": "2024-11-17T17:09:43.638Z"}, "record": {"$type": "app.bsky.feed.post", "createdAt": "2026-11-09T23:26:09.951Z", "embed": {"$type": "app.bsky.embed.images", "images": [{"alt": "Scott, and Jamaal Wilkes, were replaced in the starting lineup by coach Pat Riley, \"to inject something to get us back on track.\" Scott was 12-for-16 from the field. \"It didn't bother me. I just want him (Riley) to know he can count on me.\"\n\nFor the second time in five days, with both games against the Lakers, four Portland players topped the 20-point mark. Mychal Thompson led the way with 28 points, while also getting 7 rebounds and 8 assists on his stat line. Kiki Vandeweghe adding 25 points, with Jim Paxson adding 23 more. Clyde Drexler came off the bench to add 20 points, 7 rebounds, 9 assists, and 3 steals. Darnell Valentine added a game-high 11 assists.\n\nFor Los Angeles, after Scott, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar scored 24 and James Worthy added 21 points, with both players grabbing a team high 7 rebounds. Wilkes added 16 points, while Magic Johnson added 15 points and 15 assists. \n\nPortland coach Jack Ramsay was ejected with under two minutes remaining after receiving his second technical. Ramsay was irate during the final quarter when the first nine fouls were called on Portland, then received the ejection after Portland was called for an illegal defense. It was the first time he was ejected in a home game. \"I'm not allowed to comment on the officiating,\" said Ramsay, who will be docked $250 for the technicals.", "aspectRatio": {"height": 690, "width": 1168}, "image": {"$type": "blob", "ref": {"$link": "bafkreig4huwhdto4w5nuurbth6jkt3lfwpuauuchwdjfidxz6d4epxnhou"}, "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "size": 582093}}]}, "facets": [{"features": [{"$type": "app.bsky.richtext.facet#tag", "tag": "RipCity"}], "index": {"byteEnd": 246, "byteStart": 238}}, {"features": [{"$type": "app.bsky.richtext.facet#tag", "tag": "ThisDateinBlazersHistory"}], "index": {"byteEnd": 272, "byteStart": 247}}], "langs": ["en"], "text": "November 9, 1984 - Not starting for the first time since mid-way through his rookie year, Byron Scott came off the bench to score 27 points, including a jumper with :08 seconds to secure the Lakers 130-126 shootout against the Blazers. \n\n#RipCity #ThisDateinBlazersHistory"}, "embed": {"images": [{"thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:ixcg2jfvljshf3p7jhmt77ee/bafkreig4huwhdto4w5nuurbth6jkt3lfwpuauuchwdjfidxz6d4epxnhou", "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:ixcg2jfvljshf3p7jhmt77ee/bafkreig4huwhdto4w5nuurbth6jkt3lfwpuauuchwdjfidxz6d4epxnhou", "alt": "Scott, and Jamaal Wilkes, were replaced in the starting lineup by coach Pat Riley, \"to inject something to get us back on track.\" Scott was 12-for-16 from the field. \"It didn't bother me. I just want him (Riley) to know he can count on me.\"\n\nFor the second time in five days, with both games against the Lakers, four Portland players topped the 20-point mark. Mychal Thompson led the way with 28 points, while also getting 7 rebounds and 8 assists on his stat line. Kiki Vandeweghe adding 25 points, with Jim Paxson adding 23 more. Clyde Drexler came off the bench to add 20 points, 7 rebounds, 9 assists, and 3 steals. Darnell Valentine added a game-high 11 assists.\n\nFor Los Angeles, after Scott, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar scored 24 and James Worthy added 21 points, with both players grabbing a team high 7 rebounds. Wilkes added 16 points, while Magic Johnson added 15 points and 15 assists. \n\nPortland coach Jack Ramsay was ejected with under two minutes remaining after receiving his second technical. Ramsay was irate during the final quarter when the first nine fouls were called on Portland, then received the ejection after Portland was called for an illegal defense. It was the first time he was ejected in a home game. \"I'm not allowed to comment on the officiating,\" said Ramsay, who will be docked $250 for the technicals.", "aspectRatio": {"height": 690, "width": 1168}}], "$type": "app.bsky.embed.images#view"}, "bookmarkCount": 0, "replyCount": 0, "repostCount": 0, "likeCount": 0, "quoteCount": 0, "indexedAt": "2026-11-09T23:26:12.278Z", "labels": []}, {"uri": "at://did:plc:ywsla6rhibn7h3w6oi6sgkrc/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzw364snmu2g", "cid": "bafyreia7ctijbomwmtfm5ugfxodqkzyjri5epft7h6b32jlsaox6j74wha", "author": {"did": "did:plc:ywsla6rhibn7h3w6oi6sgkrc", "handle": "nbarealtimestats.bsky.social", "displayName": "NBA Realtime Stats", "avatar": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ywsla6rhibn7h3w6oi6sgkrc/bafkreicch7wq2uorzqbeoaom3wn6pb627u4sftummbu7itbeo7sk63u3ne", "associated": {"activitySubscription": {"allowSubscriptions": "followers"}}, "labels": [], "createdAt": "2024-11-15T11:53:40.921Z"}, "record": {"$type": "app.bsky.feed.post", "createdAt": "2026-11-09T23:25:47.577322+00:00", "langs": ["en"], "text": "\ud83c\udfc0 Coming up: LAL @ ATL \u2014 8:00 PM ET\n\n#NBA #Hawks #Lakers"}, "bookmarkCount": 0, "replyCount": 0, "repostCount": 0, "likeCount": 0, "quoteCount": 0, "indexedAt": "2026-11-09T23:25:48.579Z", "labels": []}, {"uri": "at://did:plc:m3fplcau4gtobxb3li5wgikd/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzw2m544a52p", "cid": "bafyreia3dplygbzu4b7gth5mq5vcsbkvlsyfurg55ck4zk46m3yazglj4u", "author": {"did": "did:plc:m3fplcau4gtobxb3li5wgikd", "handle": "realnba.com", "displayName": "RealNBA", "avatar": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:m3fplcau4gtobxb3li5wgikd/bafkreic3ag7lkdsfarp3s56bcfcflyiybtgusavg2nwb6hcffw2nxpg55u", "associated": {"activitySubscription": {"allowSubscriptions": "followers"}}, "labels": [{"src": "did:plc:m3fplcau4gtobxb3li5wgikd", "uri": "at://did:plc:m3fplcau4gtobxb3li5wgikd/app.bsky.actor.profile/self", "cid": "bafyreifssq6ihli7me2wsiaxvsbek4rp5fsjj7